From 1a839dd1e82670083cf861e3704dea6bf4141dae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:30:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 042/100] scripting: localStorage persists, as SceneScript's
 ILocalStorage

localStorage was an in-memory object that stored String(value), had
no delete and no locations. Now:

- get/set/delete/clear (key, location), LOCATION_GLOBAL ("global") and
  LOCATION_SCREEN ("screen", the default). delete answers whether the
  key was there; remove stays as LWE's old name for it.
- Values keep their type (JSON): a number comes back a number, an
  object an object, and a stored Vec2/Vec3/Vec4 a vector again. A
  missing key reads undefined (WE's result is not documented; the
  library's scripts read it with || or ??).
- It persists: new wp_config_set_storage_dir names a directory, and
  each project keeps one JSON file there (its Workshop id, else its
  title), written whole and renamed after a tick that changed it, and
  when the scene goes. Over WE's 100 KB it is not saved (logged).
  Without a directory it lives as long as the scene, as before.
- One "screen" store per project: the core plays a project on one
  screen.

Origin: ours
Why: saved positions and settings reset on every start (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B10: S36)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8XbjUdhpEVfhFbe7bj
